# Hybrid Fly cost rail (AuthorForge + StoryForge)

ScanLogic stays on Vercel. Studios on Fly use **auto-stop** machines. Every cold hit to
`*.fly.dev` (page load, `/health`, deploy smoke) can **start a machine** and burn trial
(7 days **or** 2h runtime) / pay-as-you-go credits.

Treat Fly runtime like API keys: **default deny** unnecessary use.

## Non-negotiables

1. **Do not wake production Fly** unless the user explicitly asked to deploy, debug prod, or open the live studio.
2. Prefer **local** studios (`authorforge` / `storyforge` `npm run …:dev`, FakeLLM / mock images) for agent work, tests, and UI iteration.
3. **Never** add background polling of Fly `/health` from ScanLogic (Hub, dashboards, intervals, prefetch on mount). Health probes only on **explicit user launch** (`launchAuthorforgeDesktop` / `launchStoryforgeDesktop`).
4. Do not “verify” prod by looping `curl …/health`, opening both studios, or refreshing studio tabs during agent sessions.
5. Keep `fly.toml`: `auto_stop_machines = "stop"`, `auto_start_machines = true`, `min_machines_running = 0` unless the user explicitly wants always-on (and accepts cost).
6. Do not allocate dedicated IPv4, extra machines, Redis, Postgres, or second regions “just in case.”
7. Production secrets stay on Fly (`fly secrets`); never put studio secrets in `VITE_*`.
8. After intentional prod smoke: one `/health` per app is enough — then stop.

## When Fly wake *is* allowed

- User asked to deploy / set secrets / fix a prod outage
- User is actively testing the live URL
- Single post-deploy smoke: `curl …/health` once per app

## Agent checklist before any `fly` / `*.fly.dev` action

- [ ] User requested prod/Fly explicitly?
- [ ] Can this be done locally with mock/fake?
- [ ] Will this start a stopped machine? If yes, minimize to one request.
- [ ] Avoid leaving `fly logs` / `fly ssh` sessions open.

## Parallel to LLM/API key discipline

| Cost surface | Default | Prod use |
|--------------|---------|----------|
| Anthropic / fal / Replicate | fake/mock in tests; no drive-by live calls | only when implementing/debugging paid path |
| Fly machines | local hybrid / stopped | only intentional deploy, smoke, or user launch |

